On Jan 8, 7:03 pm, Jistan Idiot <jistanid...@gmail.com> wrote:
> She's got this really cool hammer, Mjollnir.  While it seems to be the
> ultimate killing weapon, it has one tiny little side effect.   It
> seems to blow up wands that the monsters have.  In fact it just blew
> up a /oDeath and I really need to figure out how to avoid it from
> doing that.

As a lawful you can dip a long sword in fountains to
get Excalibur, which does an extra 1d10 damage to
*any* monster, as opposed to Mjollnir's 1d24 damage
to non-shock resistant monsters.  (Many monsters on
Astral etc. are shock resistant.)  Plus it won't blow up
rings and wands with its lightning attack.

> She also has a problem with fending off curses from the liches and
> other curse casting nasties.

They respect Elbereth, so burn E on the upstairs and you
should be good to go.  Or you could just genocide them.
Disenchanters also respect Elbereth, by the way.

